# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# ASan/UBSan/LSan suppressions for the nightly `asan` lane (issue #702,
# docs/specs/memory-model-v1.md section 10).
#
# Format: one entry per line, `interceptor:pattern`, preceded by a `#` comment line that gives the
# reason. The sanitizer runtime ignores blank lines and `#` comments.
#
# POLICY - read before adding a line:
#   * Tessera's own code is NEVER suppressed here. If our code trips ASan, UBSan or LSan, that is a
#     finding to report and fix, not to silence. The lane exists to surface it.
#   * Only a third-party library may be listed, and only with a reason that names the library, the
#     report it emits and why the report is not ours to fix.
#
# CURRENT STATE: one entry, for Mesa's lavapipe software Vulkan driver. It is the only third-party
# report the full suite produces; everything else the lane found was Tessera's own code and was
# fixed rather than suppressed.

# Mesa lavapipe (libvulkan_lvp.so), the software Vulkan ICD the Linux lane renders with. When a test
# forces a device or texture-pool creation to fail, lavapipe leaks the partially built object: the
# whole allocation stack is inside `libvulkan_lvp.so`, and the only Tessera frame is the call that
# asked for the object. It is not ours to fix, and it is not a Tessera defect - the leak is the
# driver's own error path, which the test triggers on purpose. Matched on the module name so a leak
# with Tessera frames in it is still reported.
leak:libvulkan_lvp.so
